rt of the inspiration as well but  aside from that I'm just filling in some  of the foothills here with some more  houses and that is basically it I added  one more Island over here I'm going to  add another Island on the other side of  the main island as well just to add  something to the sides but that's really  just about it and I also have to say  with the size of this this whole build  I'm almost running out of space like on  this side I'm actually running into the  world border and I'm also running into  the world border almost on the other  side space is very limited in this game  and you can't build huge sprawling  metropolis so that's something to keep  in mind but yeah with that said let's  take a quick look and how the final  products are inside all right so this is  the results of about two hours of work  so all things considered you can build  some pretty cool stuff in a very short  amount of time  but of course I also think this is not  really a game where the final product is  the focus it's more so just fun to build  stuff but yeah I at least want to  showcase it a little bit and I do like  how the the central castle does have a  bit of a body to it I figured out that  even though if you put roofs together  it normally creates a flat surface like  this one way to get around that is to  intersect it with higher sections of  roof like over here so I managed to get  a pointy roof on top of this whole  castle section bit here just by having  the tower kind of intersected and this  thing as well so that's something to  keep in mind there are always ways that  you can like sort of game this system  the Creator actually tweeted something  today there are nearly 500 different  sort of puzzle pieces that make up all  of the building blocks of this game  and the a I just kind of has to figure  out what kind of puzzle pieces to get  together depending on which building  blocks you're putting together but it  sometimes makes some really cool  combination so for instance I made these  little gateways just by putting some  blocks together it automatically makes  these slopes roofs going to the middle  here and then you just have this or  gable up front so obviously I don't know  all of the combinations of what building  blocks turn into when you put them  together yet but clearly there's  actually been some thought put into how  building blocks go together and what  you're trying to build and the game  really adjusts for a lot so one of my  favorite examples is actually the  entrance gates over here which is at the  sort of make-believe Harbor section with  a bunch of pigeons on the roof where you  could sell that on the bottom we have  these arches and it goes from iron  pillars into the stone arches for this  building piece here and then because  there's a separate building block which  actually is kind of unconnected to any  other building blocks but it does have  building blocks to the left and the  right underneath it it automatically  creates an arch over here as well and  then of course we have the spires on the  side so even though you only have one  building block and you just kind of  click everywhere you really get a large  variety of shapes and that is not even  to mention how the grid effects the  shape of things as well so for instance  on the side here and oh god the camera  is actually being a bit difficult with  me here because the world borders here  but on the side here we have a very big  writ space making this fire and a very  small and making this fire so you  definitely get a lot of variety that way  as well but even with that and with the  very uneven grid which is curvy at times  you also still have a lot of control  over how things look so altogether I  think it's really well balanced between  you know giving the player control over  how things look and taking the Krone the  control away from you to figure out how  to make things look as good as possible  I think the game strikes a really good  balance  and honestly I would personally  recommend this game if you're interested  in city building or creative games or  the kind of doodling game that this is  of course if you're interested in actual  gameplay I wouldn't recommend it this is  really all there is to it it's a very  simple game at least at the moment it's  still an early access of course so that  might also be a reason why you want to  wait with purchasing this game even if  you're interested in it  but I think for me my personal  conclusion is that this this little toy  if you will it doesn't do much but what  it does it does really well and for what  it is which is essentially just a  glorified doodling tool it's really  great the sound design is very  satisfying the way that everything comes  together and how the game figures out  what to turn buildings into is very  satisfying and the art style is just  really charming the colors of it all it  just works really well together and I  think the main thing is that with some  creative games it can be hard sometimes  to make something that you're happy with  sometimes you're just looking at what  you're building being very disappointed  by it and it's just demotivating this  game just makes it so easy to make nice  looking things and sure whatever you're  building doesn't have to look like this  it can be completely different as well  anyway but so far I've just noticed that  I can honestly just put down random  stuff and not really think about it too  much and still look back at it and think  hmm that's pretty neat and for that I  have to give this game props so that's  basically my conclusion I really like it  so far the game has a really great  foundation and I'm very curious to see  where it will go in the future if you're  already intrigued by this and you like  the kind of doodling too I would highly  recommend it otherwise wait for the  future and see what else gets added to  this if anything and I have to give a  final shout out to jazz and Mary from  City skylines who let me know about this  game's release as soon as it did and  because my friend Bob tweeted about this  and got likes for it I need to say don't  forget to Like and subscribe and click  that Bell to become part of the  notification squad I've never done calls  to action it it just feels strange I  feel like a weird person doing this but  I guess I have to do it now anyway this  one's for you Bob I guess I'll see you  guys in the next game or perhaps in the  future in another time scape or video  take care to stay safe and hope you have  a good day
 

